Changes in this fork
--------------------
2026-10 — seller roles (AuctionHouseBot.Sellers / SellerShares): Materials, Crafted and Gear
          characters each own a share of every house's listing cap.
2026-10 — pricing table (new src/AHBotPricing.*, src/AHBotRoles.*): crafted items priced from
          their reagents (+ CraftMarkup, never below the original formula); non-crafted gear
          calibrated against crafted gear of the same quality/item level; materials keep the
          original formula. The buyer pays a fixed price clamped below the seller's floor.
2026-10 — .ahbot price command; public AuctionHouseBot::GetItemPricing API (used by
          mod-ahbot-price and, through it, mod-enchanter-npc).
2026-10 — bot listings' start bid is floored just above the buyer's price, so winning a bot
          auction at its start bid and reselling it to the buyer bot always loses money.
2026-10 — scarcest-first listing (AuctionHouseBot.ListScarcestOfCandidates): each fresh listing
          picks the item category by ListProportion weight as before, then draws K candidates
          from within it and lists the one with the fewest current listings in that house, so
          per-item stock depth evens out inside each category instead of varying by luck.
